WEBVTT - Weekly platform sync

NOTE
Transcribed locally by Hansard. No data left the organisation.

1
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:14.600
<v Amara Okafor>Good morning everyone, let us start with
the release four point two readiness.</v>

2
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:20.674
<v Léa Fontaine>The build is green on every runner, but
the German locale files still have forty</v>

3
00:00:20.674 --> 00:00:24.900
<v Léa Fontaine>seven untranslated strings and nobody has
proof-read them yet.</v>

4
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:29.100
Sorry, could you repeat the last figure?

5
00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:33.000
<v Léa Fontaine>Forty seven strings, all of them in the
billing screens.</v>

6
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.400
<v Amara Okafor>Understood.</v>

7
00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:16.234
<v Amara Okafor>Then we ship four point two on the twelfth
of June with the German locale disabled,</v>

8
00:06:16.234 --> 00:06:19.800
<v Amara Okafor>and we open a follow-up ticket for the
translations.</v>

9
00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:46.355
<v Jonas Weber>On the incident of last Tuesday: the pager
fired at two in the morning, the responder</v>

10
00:10:46.355 --> 00:10:51.500
<v Jonas Weber>had already worked a full week, and the
hand-over notes were missing.</v>

11
00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:38.400
<v Amara Okafor>Agreed, we move the rotation to a two-week
cycle starting in July.</v>

12
00:19:40.000 --> 00:19:47.000
<v Léa Fontaine>For the transcription cluster we need two
more GPU nodes to keep the queue under ten</v>

13
00:19:47.713 --> 00:19:49.200
<v Léa Fontaine>minutes at peak.</v>

14
00:23:45.000 --> 00:23:51.800
<v Amara Okafor>Approved. Please draft the procurement
request before the board meeting.</v>
